From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:38:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: a flip keeps the RGB range that the mode set of the
 head asked for

A flip that changes the HDR state of a head (dirty.hdr in
UpdateProposedFlipStateOneApiHead()) chose its range again from the range
of the dpy, requestedColorRange, which no client of Hades sets: full range.
A head that its mode set had made limited range (nvidia-drm's "Broadcast
RGB" "Limited 16:235", KAPI hadesColorRangeLimited, colorRangeSpecified of
the request) went back to full range with such a flip, its range
compression off and its AVI InfoFrame saying full range, while nvidia-drm
and Kodi still had it limited; nothing set it right before the next mode
set that changed the range.

The flips of Hades that have new HDR state, read in KAPI and nvidia-drm:
- every flip that disables a layer: nvidia-drm marks its output transfer
  function and its HDR metadata changed (plane_req_config_disable()), and
  KAPI passes both (tf and layer hdr specified);
- a flip that changes NV_HDR_STATIC_METADATA of a plane, or its output
  transfer function;
- in 615, on a GPU whose InfoFrames go with the flip (SetCoreFid, the C6
  HAL, with HDMI connectors only), the start and the end of HDR10, a new HDR
  InfoFrame (also the end of HDR asked for again) and a new colorimetry,
  which KAPI sends as flips there; elsewhere, and always in 580, those are
  mode sets and were not affected.
Not affected: the HDR10+ VSIF of each frame (580: its own ioctl; 615:
dirty.hdmiVsifMetadata, not dirty.hdr), the start and the end of Dolby
Vision with "Limited 16:235" (a change of hadesColorRangeLimited is a mode
set), and Kodi's own and half-float buffers (a new surface, not new HDR
state).

The api-head state now keeps what its last mode set asked for
(hadesColorRangeSpecified, hadesColorRange, set in
ApplyProposedModeSetStateOneApiHeadPreUpdate(), cleared when the head is
shut down), and the flip chooses from it (HadesFlipRequestedColorRange()):
a head whose mode set asked for limited range stays limited; one that asked
for nothing ("Automatic", "Full", and the Dolby Vision tunnel, which
nvidia-drm leaves to NVKMS's full range) takes the range of the dpy, as
before; YCbCr stays limited either way. The line of the kernel's log for
each change of the range compression of a head (nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9058) shows that a
flip no longer changes it.

Tested on the host: the flip's choice with the code of each tree
(flip_extract.py takes the helper, the argument of the call in the flip,
the statements of the mode set that store the range, and
nvChooseColorRangeEvo() as they are): 7 of 7 with this change, 2 of 7
failing with the tree before it (limited range put back to full), 4 of 4
mutations caught; the NVKMS core of both trees built with the image's
compiler, no new warning. Not run on a GPU.
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h |  9 ++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-flip.c      | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c   |  7 ++++++
 3 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
index e4f5806..72e27f0 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
@@ -2098,6 +2098,15 @@ typedef struct _NVDispApiHeadStateEvoRec {
     } rgSemaInfo;
 
     NvBool postcompColorPassthrough : 1;
+    /*
+     * Hades: the RGB range that the last mode set of this api-head asked
+     * for (NvKmsSetModeOneHeadRequest::colorRangeSpecified, which KAPI sets
+     * from nvidia-drm's "Broadcast RGB", hadesColorRangeLimited), and
+     * whether it asked for one: a flip that changes the HDR state of the
+     * head keeps it (UpdateProposedFlipStateOneApiHead()).
+     */
+    NvBool hadesColorRangeSpecified;
+    enum NvKmsDpyAttributeColorRangeValue hadesColorRange;
 } NVDispApiHeadStateEvoRec;
 
 typedef struct _NVDispVblankApiHeadState {
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-flip.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-flip.c
index b7c4476..67dddbf 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-flip.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-flip.c
@@ -148,6 +148,30 @@ static void FillPostSyncptReplyOneApiHead(
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the RGB range that a flip which changes the HDR state of a head
+ * chooses from (nvChooseColorRangeEvo()). NVKMS took the range of the dpy
+ * (requestedColorRange: full range, as no client of Hades sets that
+ * attribute), so that such a flip put a head that its mode set had made
+ * limited range (nvidia-drm's "Broadcast RGB" "Limited 16:235", KAPI
+ * hadesColorRangeLimited) back to full range, with its AVI InfoFrame, while
+ * nvidia-drm and Kodi still had it limited: the flip that starts or ends
+ * HDR10 where the GPU writes InfoFrames with the flip (615), one that changes
+ * the transfer function or the HDR metadata of a layer, and every flip that
+ * disables a layer (nvidia-drm marks its transfer function and its HDR
+ * metadata changed). The range that the mode set asked for is kept; a head
+ * whose mode set asked for none ("Automatic", "Full", and the Dolby Vision
+ * tunnel, which nvidia-drm keeps in NVKMS's full range) takes the range of
+ * the dpy, as before. YCbCr stays limited range either way.
+ */
+static enum NvKmsDpyAttributeColorRangeValue HadesFlipRequestedColorRange(
+    const NVDispApiHeadStateEvoRec *pApiHeadState,
+    const NVDpyEvoRec *pDpyEvo)
+{
+    return pApiHeadState->hadesColorRangeSpecified ?
+        pApiHeadState->hadesColorRange : pDpyEvo->requestedColorRange;
+}
+
 static NvBool UpdateProposedFlipStateOneApiHead(
     const NVDispEvoRec *pDispEvo,
     const NvU32 apiHead,
@@ -245,7 +269,8 @@ static NvBool UpdateProposedFlipStateOneApiHead(
             }
         }
 
-        nvChooseColorRangeEvo(pDpyEvo->requestedColorRange,
+        nvChooseColorRangeEvo(HadesFlipRequestedColorRange(pApiHeadState,
+                                                           pDpyEvo),
                               pProposedApiHead->hdr.dpyColor.format,
                               pProposedApiHead->hdr.dpyColor.bpc,
                               &pProposedApiHead->hdr.dpyColor.range);
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
index c49d554..80971fc 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
@@ -2893,6 +2893,8 @@ ApplyProposedModeSetStateOneApiHeadShutDown(
     nvkms_memset(&pApiHeadState->modeValidationParams, 0,
                  sizeof(pApiHeadState->modeValidationParams));
     nvkms_memset(&pApiHeadState->timings, 0, sizeof(pApiHeadState->timings));
+    /* Hades: a head that is shut down has no range asked for */
+    pApiHeadState->hadesColorRangeSpecified = FALSE;
     nvkms_memset(&pApiHeadState->stereo, 0, sizeof(pApiHeadState->stereo));
 
     pDpyEvo->apiHead = NV_INVALID_HEAD;
@@ -3439,6 +3441,11 @@ ApplyProposedModeSetStateOneApiHeadPreUpdate(
                                                proposedPrimaryHead, updateState);
 
     pApiHeadState->attributes = pProposedApiHead->attributes;
+    /* Hades: the range that this mode set asked for, which flips keep */
+    pApiHeadState->hadesColorRangeSpecified =
+        pProposedApiHead->colorRangeSpecified;
+    pApiHeadState->hadesColorRange =
+        pProposedApiHead->attributes.color.range;
     pApiHeadState->tf = pProposedApiHead->tf;
     pApiHeadState->hdrInfoFrameOverride =
         pProposedApiHead->hdrInfoFrameOverride;
